---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="CGP — Governed context for AI"
  description="CGP is the open protocol and runtime for private, policy-bound and provable AI context."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Open protocol · Pre-alpha</span>
        <h1>Control what AI <span class="gradient-text">can know and use.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">
          CGP is the governed context layer between your data and AI models. It selects what is necessary, removes what is sensitive, enforces policy and records why every decision was made.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="/getting-started/quick-start/">Start building →</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/docs/">Explore documentation</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-proof" aria-label="Project properties">
          <span>Apache-2.0</span>
          <span>Model agnostic</span>
          <span>Privacy first</span>
          <span>MCP compatible direction</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="governance-console" aria-label="CGP governance pipeline preview">
        <div class="console-bar">
          <div class="console-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="console-title">cgp / context-resolution</span>
          <span class="console-status">POLICY ACTIVE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="console-body">
          <div class="context-request">
            <div class="context-request-head">
              <strong>legal-document-summary</strong>
              <span>request_0193</span>
            </div>
            <div class="contract-grid">
              <div class="contract-item"><small>privacy</small><strong>anonymous-only</strong></div>
              <div class="contract-item"><small>jurisdiction</small><strong>EU</strong></div>
              <div class="contract-item"><small>token budget</small><strong>8,000</strong></div>
              <div class="contract-item"><small>retention</small><strong>zero</strong></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="pipeline-list">
            <div class="pipeline-row">
              <span class="pipeline-icon">01</span>
              <span><strong>Local privacy scan</strong><small>12 identifiers transformed</small></span>
              <span class="pipeline-result">PASSED</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pipeline-row">
              <span class="pipeline-icon">02</span>
              <span><strong>Context planning</strong><small>62% irrelevant context omitted</small></span>
              <span class="pipeline-result">PLANNED</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pipeline-row">
              <span class="pipeline-icon">03</span>
              <span><strong>Provider policy</strong><small>EU processing · zero retention</small></span>
              <span class="pipeline-result review">REVIEWED</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span>Evidence bundle generated</span>
            <strong>receipt:7f0a…9c2e</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">The governed context stack</span>
        <h2>One control plane for context, privacy and trust.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Replace scattered prompt filters, document scrubbing and provider-specific rules with a portable contract enforced before inference.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento-grid">
      <a class="bento-card wide accent" href="/concepts/context-contract/">
        <div class="card-orbit"><i></i></div>
        <div class="card-top"><span class="card-index">01 / CONTRACT</span><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></div>
        <h3>Declare exactly what the model is allowed to receive.</h3>
        <p>Intent, token and byte budgets, freshness, provenance, privacy level, jurisdiction and retention become machine-readable constraints.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="bento-card purple" href="/privacy/local-gateway/">
        <div class="card-top"><span class="card-index">02 / PRIVACY</span><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></div>
        <h3>Sanitize before transmission.</h3>
        <p>Extract and transform documents locally. Unsupported or insufficiently inspected content can fail closed.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="bento-card" href="/architecture/overview/">
        <div class="card-top"><span class="card-index">03 / PLANNING</span><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></div>
        <h3>Compile the minimum sufficient context.</h3>
        <p>Rank context nodes under explicit token, byte, freshness and latency budgets instead of sending full document dumps.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="bento-card" href="/security/trust-firewall/">
        <div class="card-top"><span class="card-index">04 / TRUST</span><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></div>
        <h3>Keep data from becoming instructions.</h3>
        <p>Untrusted files, web content and tool output cannot promote themselves into policies, permissions or executable actions.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="bento-card half" href="/governance/eu-compliance/">
        <div class="card-top"><span class="card-index">05 / GOVERNANCE</span><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></div>
        <h3>Turn requirements into deterministic decisions.</h3>
        <p>CGP targets five runtime outcomes: ALLOW, SANITIZE, ROUTE_LOCAL, REQUIRE_HUMAN and DENY.</p>
      </a>

      <a class="bento-card half accent" href="/reference/receipts/">
        <div class="card-top"><span class="card-index">06 / EVIDENCE</span><span class="card-arrow">↗</span></div>
        <h3>Prove what happened without exposing the original secrets.</h3>
        <p>Portable receipts capture context, transformations, routing and policy decisions for audit and debugging.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Request lifecycle</span>
        <h2>From raw source to authorized context.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-lead">Every stage has an explicit trust boundary and a documented output. Select any stage to inspect its design.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pipeline-grid">
      <a class="pipeline-step" href="/privacy/local-gateway/"><small>01</small><strong>Inspect</strong><span>Parse source locally</span></a>
      <a class="pipeline-step" href="/privacy/anonymization/"><small>02</small><strong>Sanitize</strong><span>Remove sensitive data</span></a>
      <a class="pipeline-step" href="/concepts/context-graph/"><small>03</small><strong>Structure</strong><span>Create context nodes</span></a>
      <a class="pipeline-step" href="/architecture/request-lifecycle/"><small>04</small><strong>Plan</strong><span>Enforce budgets</span></a>
      <a class="pipeline-step" href="/security/trust-firewall/"><small>05</small><strong>Authorize</strong><span>Apply trust and policy</span></a>
      <a class="pipeline-step" href="/reference/receipts/"><small>06</small><strong>Prove</strong><span>Generate receipts</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">CGP + MCP</span>
        <h2>Connectivity and governance are different layers.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-lead">MCP exposes tools and resources. CGP governs the context compiled from them before that context reaches a model.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="comparison">
      <div class="comparison-row"><div>Concern</div><div>MCP</div><div>CGP</div></div>
      <div class="comparison-row"><div>Primary question</div><div>What is available?</div><div class="highlight">What may be used now?</div></div>
      <div class="comparison-row"><div>Context budgets</div><div>Host-defined</div><div class="highlight">Protocol contract</div></div>
      <div class="comparison-row"><div>Local anonymization</div><div>Outside core scope</div><div class="highlight">First-class gateway</div></div>
      <div class="comparison-row"><div>Purpose and jurisdiction</div><div>Application logic</div><div class="highlight">Governance primitives</div></div>
      <div class="comparison-row"><div>Decision evidence</div><div>Implementation-specific</div><div class="highlight">Portable receipts</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/integrations/mcp/">Read the integration model →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="cta-panel">
      <div>
        <h2>Build the open standard for governed AI context.</h2>
        <p>Use the reference implementation, contribute to the protocol or fund independent open-source development.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/getting-started/quick-start/">Quick start</a>
        <a class="button button-sponsor" href="/donations/">Support CGP</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
